# What the data layer's own commands read.
#
# Bun loads `.env` files from the working directory and does not search upwards, so
# this file is what `bun run --filter @signet/db test`,
# `cd packages/db && bun run test` and the `db:*` scripts read - all of them run
# here. Commands run from the repository root read the root `.env.example` instead.
#
# The two variables go in different files, and that is Bun's rule rather than a
# convention: `bun test` sets NODE_ENV=test, and Bun does not load `.env.local` in
# that mode - it loads `.env` and `.env.test`. So the suites' variable goes in
# `.env.test` and the `db:*` scripts' goes in `.env.local`.
#
# They are also not interchangeable values. `drizzle-kit` addresses the development
# database; the suites truncate theirs.

# --- .env.local --------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by `db:migrate` and `db:studio`, and by nothing else here. `db:generate` diffs
# the schema modules against the recorded snapshot and needs no database.
#
# drizzle.config.ts falls back to `postgres://signet:signet@localhost:5432/signet`
# when this is unset, so a development database on any other host or port must be
# named here or those two commands will quietly address the wrong server.
SIGNET_DATABASE_URL=postgres://signet_app:signet_app@localhost:5432/signet

# --- .env.test ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The throwaway database the suites may migrate, create roles in and truncate. Named
# by an identity that owns the schema: the preload creates a non-owning serving role
# from it and every suite connects as that, because Postgres exempts a table's owner
# from the table's row-level security policies and a suite running exempt is not
# evidence that the policies work.
#
# Leaving it unset does not fail the run - the integration suites skip themselves, and
# the run reports success having exercised no database at all. Check for a `skip`
# count if you are not sure it is being read.
SIGNET_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://signet:signet@localhost:5432/signet
